WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.933
John, Chapter Twenty-One.

2
00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:10.000
After these things Jesus shewed himself again to the disciples at the sea of Tiberias; and on this wise shewed he himself.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.200
There were together Simon Peter, and Thomas called Didymus, and Nathanael of Cana in Galilee, and the sons of Zebedee, and two other of his disciples.

4
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.533
Simon Peter saith unto them, I go a fishing.

5
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:25.733
They say unto him, We also go with thee.

6
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:30.800
They went forth, and entered into a ship immediately; and that night they caught nothing.

7
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:37.733
But when the morning was now come, Jesus stood on the shore: but the disciples knew not that it was Jesus.

8
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:41.600
Then Jesus saith unto them, Children, have ye any meat?

9
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.467
They answered him, No.

10
00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:48.000
And he said unto them, Cast the net on the right side of the ship, and ye shall find.

11
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.800
They cast therefore, and now they were not able to draw it for the multitude of fishes.

12
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.733
Therefore that disciple whom Jesus loved saith unto Peter, It is the Lord.

13
00:00:57.733 --> 00:01:05.733
Now when Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he girt his fisher's coat unto him, (for he was naked,) and did cast himself into the sea.

14
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:14.667
And the other disciples came in a little ship; (for they were not far from land, but as it were two hundred cubits,) dragging the net with fishes.

15
00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:21.200
As soon then as they were come to land, they saw a fire of coals there, and fish laid thereon, and bread.

16
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.000
Jesus saith unto them, Bring of the fish which ye have now caught.

17
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:35.733
Simon Peter went up, and drew the net to land full of great fishes, an hundred and fifty and three: and for all there were so many, yet was not the net broken.

18
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:38.267
Jesus saith unto them, Come and dine.

19
00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:42.400
And none of the disciples durst ask him, Who art thou?

20
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.000
knowing that it was the Lord.

21
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.467
Jesus then cometh, and taketh bread, and giveth them, and fish likewise.

22
00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:55.200
This is now the third time that Jesus shewed himself to his disciples, after that he was risen from the dead.

23
00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:01.467
So when they had dined, Jesus saith to Simon Peter, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me more than these?

24
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:06.133
He saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee.

25
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.533
He saith unto him, Feed my lambs.

26
00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:14.000
He saith to him again the second time, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me?

27
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.133
He saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee.

28
00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.667
He saith unto him, Feed my sheep.

29
00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:25.200
He saith unto him the third time, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me?

30
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.733
Peter was grieved because he said unto him the third time, Lovest thou me?

31
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:34.267
And he said unto him, Lord, thou knowest all things; thou knowest that I love thee.

32
00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:37.200
Jesus saith unto him, Feed my sheep.

33
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:52.800
Verily, verily, I say unto thee, When thou wast young, thou girdedst thyself, and walkedst whither thou wouldest: but when thou shalt be old, thou shalt stretch forth thy hands, and another shall gird thee, and carry thee whither thou wouldest not.

34
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.333
This spake he, signifying by what death he should glorify God.

35
00:02:57.333 --> 00:03:01.333
And when he had spoken this, he saith unto him, Follow me.

36
00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:12.267
Then Peter, turning about, seeth the disciple whom Jesus loved following; which also leaned on his breast at supper, and said, Lord, which is he that betrayeth thee?

37
00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:17.467
Peter seeing him saith to Jesus, Lord, and what shall this man do?

38
00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:23.067
Jesus saith unto him, If I will that he tarry till I come, what is that to thee?

39
00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:24.533
follow thou me.

40
00:03:24.533 --> 00:03:38.400
Then went this saying abroad among the brethren, that that disciple should not die: yet Jesus said not unto him, He shall not die; but, If I will that he tarry till I come, what is that to thee?

41
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:46.000
This is the disciple which testifieth of these things, and wrote these things: and we know that his testimony is true.

42
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:55.067
And there are also many other things which Jesus did, the which, if they should be written every one, I suppose that even the world itself could not contain the books that should be written.

43
00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:55.733
Amen.

